# What never belongs in a build context.
#
# Nothing in the Dockerfile copies these, but the whole context is handed to the daemon before any COPY is evaluated: 13 GB of build output was being sent to build a 176 MB image, and the owner's CV and database dumps were going with it.
#
# release-image.sh builds from the reviewed commit's tracked files, so for a release most of this
# can never be present. It still applies to every other build, and a pattern here is anchored at the
# context root: `*.key` alone would have let config/server.key through, which is why the secret
# patterns all start with **/.

# Personal data and local evidence, wherever a component wrote it.
private/
**/private/
backups/
**/*.dump
**/*.dump.sha256
**/*.pdf
**/*.docx
**/*.pages
**/*.rtf
**/*.log

# Secrets.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.prod.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
# Short-lived credentials google-github-actions/auth writes into the deploy job's workspace.
**/gha-creds-*.json

# Downloaded tooling and release archives. 450 MB of gcloud CLI and every image tarball ever built
# would otherwise be handed to the daemon to build an image that uses none of it.
google-cloud-sdk/
google-cloud-cli-*.tar.gz
google-cloud-cli-*.zip
dist/

# macOS resource forks.
._*
**/._*
.AppleDouble/
**/.AppleDouble/
.DS_Store

# Build output, rebuilt inside the image anyway.
target/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
apps/web/dist/

# History and tooling.
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Documentation and session material, none of which the image needs.
docs/
Self-Docs/
prompts/
*.md
!README.md
